  "articleBody": "Remodeling a foreclosed property can be an exciting project, but it’s also ripe for costly mistakes if you’re not careful. One of the biggest blunders is jumping straight to cosmetic finishes before fixing fundamental problems. You absolutely need to address drainage, structural issues, and moisture problems first. Putting new paint on a leaky wall is just asking for trouble down the road! Another common error is underestimating hidden damage. These properties often have a lot of deferred maintenance, and what looks like a small issue can quickly snowball. Always assume there's more to uncover than meets the eye and factor that into your budget. Finally, don't forget about permits. If your work changes the structure or footprint of the building, or even just certain major systems, you'll likely need one. Failing to get the right permits can lead to delays, fines, and even having to redo work. Getting a professional assessment upfront can save you a ton of headaches and money in the long run.",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
}